⚙️ 3. Optimal Approach (Two Pointer Gap)
💡 Idea
Move first pointer n+1 steps ahead
Start second at head
Move both until first reaches null
second will be just before the node to delete
❌ Issue in YOUR code
Problem 1: Gap logic is inconsistent
for (int i = 0; i <= n; i++) {
    if (first != null)
        first = first.next;
}
If n == length, this logic doesn’t correctly handle removing head
You’re silently ignoring null instead of handling it properly
Problem 2: Edge case handling is hacky
